No memory leaks were found:

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1104661/53231189-60984980-3699-11e9-823a-b3d383a2d205.png)

 i think its related the nustaq thread locals. They seem to keep huge payloads forever. All heap dumps show that the netty threads hold the big payload in a thread local.

i can control the velocity of going out of memory with the connection pool size. Huge pool means faster out of memory.

If this is true, then it would a "limited memory leak" with a size limit of connectionpoolsize * biggest payload Fixed. Thanks for report!

I suggest you to consider SnappyCodec or LZ4Codec to compress lot of text data. Seems it requires to implement own version of `org.nustaq.serialization.FSTConfiguration.StreamCoderFactory`  with proper byte array allocation management.

