I had the same problem.I found RedissonSessionRepository.RedissonSession setAttribute method are interested in the redis writes PRINCIPAL_NAME_INDEX_NAME,but the code
` if (attributeName. equals (PRINCIPAL_NAME_INDEX_NAME) | | attributeName. equals (securityPrincipalSessionAttr)) `
always false, I don't confirm this is my configuration errors or bugs, my solution is to modify the source code,
change the code
`String securityPrincipalSessionAttr = getSessionAttrNameKey (SPRING_SECURITY_CONTEXT);`
to
 `String securityPrincipalSessionAttr = SPRING_SECURITY_CONTEXT;`
Now,PRINCIPAL_NAME_INDEX_NAME key is create in redis.
I'm not sure if this change will cause any other problems, I haven't found it yet.
Hope helpful! @mrniko Thanks for adding this issue to the 3.11.1 milestone, which may be fixed as @hs20xqy said. But 1 thing I must point out is that, after The PRINCIPAL_NAME_INDEX_NAME key is added, it cannot be deleted when the expired event happened. See the code in RedissonSessionRepository.onMessage():
```java
            String id = body.split(keyPrefix)[1];
            RedissonSession session = new RedissonSession(id);
            if (session.load()) {
                session.clearPrincipal();
            }
            publishEvent(new SessionExpiredEvent(this, session));
```

The if condition will always be false, as the expired session's key has already been deleted by redis at this moment. Nevertheless, the remaining principal won't cause a problem, if you use Spring Security's maximum session management in non-exception mode. It's just a waste of space. I know it's not easy to fix, but it's annoying in my firm even for this trival waste, so I am working on using Redisson without RedissonSessionRepository, as I said in #1897. Fixed both issues.

